@@ -116,7 +116,17 @@ If the system configuration is queueing Emails, a cron job processes them.
 
 .. code-block:: php
 
-    php /path/to/mautic/bin/console messenger:consume email
+    php /path/to/mautic/bin/console messenger:consume email --time-limit=900 --memory-limit=512M
+
+The ``messenger:consume`` command runs as a long-lived worker process. Without limits, it stays alive indefinitely and its memory usage grows over time, which can eventually exhaust the server's memory. Always set a time limit and/or a memory limit so the worker exits cleanly and the next scheduled run starts a fresh process.
+
+- ``--time-limit=SECONDS`` stops the worker after the given number of seconds. Choose a value shorter than the interval between cron runs, for example ``900`` for a job that runs every 15 minutes.
+- ``--memory-limit=SIZE`` stops the worker once it exceeds the given memory usage, for example ``512M``.
+- ``--limit=N`` stops the worker after processing ``N`` messages.
+
+.. note::
+
+    If you run ``messenger:consume`` without any of these limits, the process may never terminate and can consume an increasing amount of memory until the server runs out of resources.
 
